These fixtures list probing questions, rubrics, reference items and document hashes of
BEAM. They hold the question and rubric text of the dataset, and no chat text. The
harness fetches the chat at run time.

Source: https://huggingface.co/datasets/Mohammadta/BEAM, at the revision pinned in
benchmarks/datasets/memory.py. The data is under CC BY-SA 4.0, so the questions and
rubrics here keep that license. The benchmark code
(https://github.com/mohammadtavakoli78/BEAM) is under the MIT license. The chat text
has its own terms: see benchmarks/results/NOTICE.

Selection: lite.json holds 2 probing questions on 3 messages of conversation 17. full.json
holds 100 questions, which are the first two probing questions of each of the 10
abilities for each of conversations 1, 4, 6, 13 and 17, on whole sessions.

Builder: benchmarks/fixtures/builders/memory.py. Run
"uv run python -m benchmarks.fixtures.builders.memory" to rebuild both files.
